un trained on the leaky 'observed' corpus (crop centered/sized on t0|t1, i.e. it saw the future perimeter's geometry during training) and has NEVER seen a t0-window crop -- the ONLY geometry this live pipeline can ever produce at forecast time (the future perimeter is, by definition, unknown). So every live prediction from this model is out-of-distribution relative to its own training. The measured t0-window numbers above already reflect that (they are not a surprise), but this is 'best available', not 'production-ready' -- represent it that way. The operating_point (floor=0.0, mult=0.9) is the VAL-selected connected-causal decode point; it did NOT clear the 0.50 precision floor during selection (feasible=False, val P=0.270/R=0.259) -- it's the best-F1 fallback point, not a precision-guaranteed one.","issued_at_utc":"2026-07-30 18:12:55.648757+00:00","valid_from_utc":"2026-07-30 00:00:00","valid_to_utc":"2026-07-31 00:00:00","wfigs_date_current_utc":"2026-07-30 16:23:23+00:00","pixel_size_m":30,"veg_source":"refreshed_d4","physics_source":"eikonal_fbfm40","history_n_dates":1,"degraded_history":true,"containment_pct":95,"acres_wfigs":12781.633597236289,"hour":9,"valid_at_utc":"2026-07-30 09:00:00"}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"MultiPolygon","coordinates":[[[[-112.58833,40.13769],[-112.58833,40.13742],[-112.58797,40.13742],[-112.58797,40.13661],[-112.58762,40.13661],[-112.58762,40.13742],[-112.58727,40.13742],[-112.58727,40.13607],[-112.58692,40.13607],[-112.58692,40.13661],[-112.58621,40.13634],[-112.58621,40.13742],[-112.58692,40.13715],[-112.58692,40.13796],[-112.58621,40.13769],[-112.58621,40.13823],[-112.58551,40.13823],[-112.58551,40.13877],[-112.58515,40.13877],[-112.58515,40.13823],[-112.5841,40.13823],[-112.5841,40.13904],[-112.58374,40.13904],[-112.58374,40.13823],[-112.58339,40.13823],[-112.58339,40.13985],[-112.58304,40.13985],[-112.58304,40.13931],[-112.58268,40.13931],[-112.58268,40.13985],[-112.58233,40.13985],[-112.58233,40.13931],[-112.58198