er produce at forecast time (the future perimeter is, by definition, unknown). So every live prediction from this model is out-of-distribution relative to its own training. The measured t0-window numbers above already reflect that (they are not a surprise), but this is 'best available', not 'production-ready' -- represent it that way. The operating_point (floor=0.0, mult=0.9) is the VAL-selected connected-causal decode point; it did NOT clear the 0.50 precision floor during selection (feasible=False, val P=0.270/R=0.259) -- it's the best-F1 fallback point, not a precision-guaranteed one.","issued_at_utc":"2026-07-30 18:12:55.648757+00:00","valid_from_utc":"2026-07-30 00:00:00","valid_to_utc":"2026-07-31 00:00:00","wfigs_date_current_utc":"2026-07-30 16:23:23+00:00","pixel_size_m":30,"veg_source":"refreshed_d4","physics_source":"eikonal_fbfm40","history_n_dates":1,"degraded_history":true,"containment_pct":95,"acres_wfigs":12781.633597236289,"hour":12,"valid_at_utc":"2026-07-30 12:00:00"}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"MultiPolygon","coordinates":[[[[-112.53649,40.08541],[-112.53684,40.08541],[-112.53684,40.08568],[-112.53649,40.08568],[-112.53649,40.08541]]],[[[-112.53754,40.08541],[-112.53754,40.08568],[-112.53719,40.08568],[-112.53719,40.08541],[-112.53754,40.08541]]],[[[-112.54389,40.08568],[-112.54389,40.08595],[-112.54354,40.08595],[-112.54354,40.08568],[-112.54389,40.08568]]],[[[-112.56964,40.08864],[-112.56999,40.08864],[-112.56999,40.08891],[-112.56964,40.08891],[-112.56964,40.08864]]],[[[-112.57034,40.08891],[-112.57034,40.08918],[-112.56999,40.08918],[-112.56999,40.08891],[-112.57034,40.08891]]],[[[-112.56893,40.08999],[-112.56893,40.09026],[-112.56928,40.09026],[-112.56928,40.08972],[-112.56999,40.08945],[-112.56999,40.09053],[-112.56964,40.09053],[-112.56964,40.0908],[-112.56928,40.0908],[-112.56928,40.09053],[-112.56858,40.0908],[-112.56858,40.08999],[-112.56893,40.08999]]],[[[-112.55553,40.09053],[-112.55588,40.09053],[-112.55588,40.0908],[-112.